Implement Windows.System.Threading.ThreadPoolTimer in threadpoolwinrt.

Win32Craft (the UWP->Win32 shim used by Minecraft PE 0.10.4.40) creates a
DispatcherTimer through Windows.System.Threading.ThreadPoolTimer.  Wine 11.21
implemented ThreadPool but not ThreadPoolTimer, so activation failed and the
game received no timer ticks.

The implementation creates one dedicated thread per timer
(CreateEvent + CreateThread + WaitForSingleObject) instead of using
CreateTimerQueueTimer.  That is not the most efficient design, but it is
simple and functionally correct, which is what this port needs.

Applies to Wine 11.21; changes:
  dlls/threadpoolwinrt/classes.idl
  dlls/threadpoolwinrt/main.c
  include/windows.system.threading.idl
